# CORE: interaction with the graphics backend during effect creation. For every pass, the vertex shader is created
# first and then the pixel shader, always both, passes in order, techniques in order, even after a failure.
# A shader creation can fail in three ways:
#   - the backend returns NULL (with or without an error text);
#   - the backend returns a shader AND a non-empty error text: the text is recorded in the error list but does NOT
#     make the creation fail (the success flag is only affected by missing shaders / parameters);
#   - a uniform parameter that the parser wrote into the shader text is not known to the created shader
#     ("Effect shader parameter not found" is logged at ERROR level, not added to the error list).
# If the backend error text is non-empty it is added to the error list as "Error creating shader: <text>" (position:
# the parser cursor at the end of the input). A pass without a shader fails with a logged error. The effect
# creation result is false when a shader is missing or a parameter lookup failed; the error_string returned by
# gs_effect_create is the error list at that point, so it only appears for failed creations. Shaders created so far
# are destroyed with the half-built effect.
# The backend's fake behaviour is selected with "backend ..." (see README).
backend text hash
text a
uniform float4 col = {1,1,1,1};
float4 VS() : POSITION { return col; }
float4 PS() : TARGET { return col; }
technique T1 { pass x { vertex_shader = VS(); pixel_shader = PS(); } pass y { vertex_shader = VS(); pixel_shader = PS(); } }
technique T2 { pass { vertex_shader = VS(); pixel_shader = PS(); } }
@end
echo --- normal creation (order of backend calls)
effect e1 be1.effect @text:a
echo --- backend fails the vertex shader with a message: all remaining shaders are still requested
backend fail vertex "no vertex"
effect e2 be2.effect @text:a
backend fail vertex off
echo --- backend fails the pixel shader
backend fail pixel "no pixel"
effect e3 be3.effect @text:a
backend fail pixel off
echo --- backend fails both
backend fail vertex "VERR"
backend fail pixel "PERR"
effect e4 be4.effect @text:a
backend fail vertex off
backend fail pixel off
echo --- backend returns a shader together with an error text (e.g. warnings): recorded, but the effect is created
backend warn pixel "just a warning"
effect e5 be5.effect @text:a
backend warn pixel off
echo --- ... and it is visible in the error string only when the creation fails for another reason
backend warn pixel "W: just a warning"
backend fail vertex "E: vertex failed"
effect e5b be5b.effect @text:a
backend warn pixel off
backend fail vertex off
echo --- empty error text is ignored
backend warn pixel ""
effect e6 be6.effect @text:a
backend warn pixel off
echo --- the NULL error_string argument is allowed
backend fail vertex "ignored"
effect_noerr e7 be7.effect @text:a
backend fail vertex off
echo --- backend does not know the uniform parameters (no shader_parse)
backend parse off
effect e8 be8.effect @text:a
backend parse on
echo --- a plain (non-uniform) parameter is not looked up, so a backend that knows no variables is fine
backend parse off
effect e9 be9.effect "float4 col = {1,1,1,1};\nfloat4 VS() : POSITION { return col; }\nfloat4 PS() : TARGET { return col; }\ntechnique T { pass { vertex_shader = VS(); pixel_shader = PS(); } }"
backend parse on
echo --- error text with several lines is kept verbatim
backend fail vertex "line1\nline2\n"
effect e10 be10.effect @text:a
backend fail vertex off
echo --- the failed effects left nothing behind
effect e11 be11.effect @text:a
dump e11
